eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $4$, while in the second equation it is $-12$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}3}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $12$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-12$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-8a + 4b = 5)\\cdot (3); -2a - 12b = 5\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-24a + 12b &= 15 \\\\\n-2a - 12b &= 5 \\\\\n(-24a - 2a) &= (15 + 5) \\\\\n-26a &= 20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}3}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48f8e738-0572-5121-922d-d8e38fb86c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508286} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd845b8-5401-5d60-a03b-9a759c275fb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508287} {:answer/id #uuid "a112c9cb-8d88-5623-a13e-d989a8243fa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508331} {:answer/id #uuid "f803e108-8054-582f