e multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-6}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $24$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-24$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(5a - 4b = 6)\\cdot (-6); 8a - 24b = -6\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-30a + 24b &= -36 \\\\\n8a - 24b &= -6 \\\\\n(-30a + 8a) &= (-36 - 6) \\\\\n-22a &= -42\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-6}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508298 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "621daa3f-f6bd-5b36-9874-b650477f8088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508305} {:answer/id #uuid "a2985571-dbf8-51bf-a4f9-d9b6a23fb056" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508332} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e22db4-43ce-578a-b7fc-4204d456f11a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508343} {:answer/id #uuid "ef083660-ccf2-5acb-becc-021580a075e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2e22db4-43ce-578a-b7fc-4204d456f11a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218650834