ed.\n\nTo eliminate $y$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $y$ in the first equation is $-2$, while in the second equation it is $-4$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-2}$, then the coefficient of $y$ will turn into $4$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-4$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-3x - 2y = 5)\\cdot (-2); -8x - 4y = 3\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x + 4y &= -10 \\\\\n-8x - 4y &= 3 \\\\\n(6x - 8x) &= (-10 + 3) \\\\\n-2x &= -7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $y$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-2}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508333 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11e65d3b-c190-5cd9-8a2d-a34b04008864" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508254} {:answer/id #uuid "a7cfa321-7684-5b8e-9a83-5671a3ae619b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11e65d3b-c190-5cd9-8a2d-a34b04008864" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508254} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cf2b31d-6044-5372-9c5a-c69f14f283df" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508310} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f2ef0e2-c929-5d5d-acd3-2bf9f6dee047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508289} {:answer/id #uuid "58d2767f-c4de-5274-b3c9-0c73323041ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508300} {:answer/id #uuid "86ac76c8-afa9-53b8-b8a4-1797ce46604a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508319} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f7ae80-61c0-5732-91e8-7d4017bd7623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86ac76c8-afa9-53b8-b8a4-1797ce46604a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508319} :answer-field/id #uuid "74be7076-138c-597e-b8be-bd971a1c8b20" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a2bc7b54-6c53-543f-b23a-786a9000e0b8" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{-5a - 15b = 8; -8a - 3b = 10$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $-15$, while in the second equation it is $-3$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}-5}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $15$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-15$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-5a - 15b = 8; (-8a - 3b = 10)\\cdot (-5)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5a - 15b &= 8 \\\\\n40a + 15b &= -50 \\\\\n(-5a + 40a) &= (8 - 50) \\\\\n35a &= -42\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-5}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508342 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "220d1f0d-705a-51be-82e7-454a15c207cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508263} {:answer/id #uuid "46b40b50-8f41-5621-8507-c13a24eb8d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508284} {:answer/id #uuid "9de0642e-8140-505e-bfef-fd699ee965c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508329} {:answer/id #uuid "e0cb89cc-3ada-54c1-844b-f8a94e1b7b32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "220d1f0d-705a-51be-82e7-454a15c207cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508263} :answer-field/id #uuid "0498b1cf-1084-5733-bdf4-ea8c3243f834" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/t