8313} :answer-field/id #uuid "873c2de2-15f7-503c-a9ac-a78b7c9793bb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508320}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cbd0b334-3f69-5bfe-96e0-237eb18aaf58" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$\\{a - b = -6; -7a - 3b = 9$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $-1$, while in the second equation it is $-3$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-3}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $3$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-3$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(a - b = -6)\\cdot (-3); -7a - 3b = 9\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3a + 3b &= 18 \\\\\n-7a - 3b &= 9 \\\\\n(-3a - 7a) &= (18 + 9) \\\\\n-10a &= 27\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-3}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508354 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39a6814c-18ed-51c5-ac72-0b9e8d2d7b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860