88fc" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{6x - y = 8; -6x + 2y = 6$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $y$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $y$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $y$ in the first equation is $-1$, while in the second equation it is $2$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}2}$, then the coefficient of $y$ will turn into $-2$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $2$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(6x - y = 8)\\cdot (2); -6x + 2y = 6\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12x - 2y &= 16 \\\\\n-6x + 2y &= 6 \\\\\n(12x - 6x) &= (16 + 6) \\\\\n6x &= 22\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $y$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}2}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508360 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "225d1f98-8b27-555d-afa6-e6d941ada34c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508264} {:answer/id #uuid "dc1678d3-65a7-531d-aee9-ccee73215a8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508356} {:answer/id #uuid "dfcb8d2b-1f63-5290-bbaf-e02572a87ce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218604549