orked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $4$, while in the second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}2}$, then the coefficient of $x$ will turn into $-4$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $4$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{4x - y = 7; (-2x - 2y = -6)\\cdot (2)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - y &= 7 \\\\\n-4x - 4y &= -12 \\\\\n(-y - 4y) &= (7 - 12) \\\\\n-5y &= -5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $x$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}2}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509164 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93dcc73c-ce2d-5fa3-b32b-9fc600fb269e" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the First Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77ee12f8-d1f3-570d-a553-36dadb480f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509183} {:answer/id #uuid "a65b148e-ebaa-5313-b824-fd0cb34f8f6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77ee12f8-d1f3-570d-a553-36dadb480f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509183} :answer-field/id #uuid "89a51c62-b05a-540b-9e93-1b6230dda76a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509189} {:answer-field/choices [{