ae28aa03" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{15u - 6v = -10; 3u - 8v = -12$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $u$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $u$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $u$ in the first equation is $15$, while in the second equation it is $3$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}-5}$, then the coefficient of $u$ will turn into $-15$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $15$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{15u - 6v = -10; (3u - 8v = -12)\\cdot (-5)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $u$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n15u - 6v &= -10 \\\\\n-15u + 40v &= 60 \\\\\n(-6v + 40v) &= (-10 + 60) \\\\\n34v &= 50\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $u$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-5}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93dcc73c-ce2d-5fa3-b32b-9fc600fb269e" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the First Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f820aee-0719-5afc-b3d3-14f46271246a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509128} {:answer/id #uuid "cbac78f7-7dff-51a3-a55d-073dd5230aa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f820aee-0719-5afc-b3d3-14f46271246a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ide