is $-8$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-4}$, then the coefficient of $s$ will turn into $8$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-8$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-2s + 10t = 5)\\cdot (-4); -8s - 2t = 10\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8s - 40t &= -20 \\\\\n-8s - 2t &= 10 \\\\\n(-40t - 2t) &= (-20 + 10) \\\\\n-42t &= -10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $s$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-4}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93dcc73c-ce2d-5fa3-b32b-9fc600fb269e" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the First Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19a023a1-5637-52be-becc-94d44c704a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509134} {:answer/id #uuid "2d4852eb-b287-5edc-94bd-5d263ed7b246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509143} {:answer/id #uuid "5cdd9d3f-8d36-58b4-9886-ce4ee52ed524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509163} {:answer/id #uuid "918562c7-6c5b-59ed-b9ef-27e37857cff7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cdd9d3f-8d36-58b4-9886-ce4ee52ed524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref